 "boxes": {
  "source_status": "current standard (Oregon Standard Drawings 2024, eff. 2026-06-01)",
  "geometry_notes": [
   "48 in wide boxes; TYPICAL SECTION: 5 in webs, 38 in void, 5 1/2 in top and bottom slabs, void depth = depth - 11 in, 3 x 3 in void chamfers ('3\" typ.'), square outer corners.",
   "Keyway: 6 in top band inset 3/8 in, then a 6 in key band containing the 3/8 in and 3/4 in transitions to the 3/4 in recess (convention: transitions kept inside the 6 in band as on the slab sheets; the box sheet's 3/4 in callout sits just below the band and is ambiguous; the difference is 0.28 in2 per side).",
   "Printed properties reproduced within 0.25 in2, 0.01 in c.g. and 0.06% I."
  ],
